WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.255
And many people might
like and want to help you,

00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:06.320
especially if they have
received help from you.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.820
Giving and receiving support often
makes people feel closer to each other.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.164
But before you give up on the idea
of social support coping,

00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:18.260
please continue with this section
to hear a little more information.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:25.410
Think about what kinds of support
you are comfortable asking of others.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.311
It is important to be
aware of your comfort

00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:31.290
zone about seeking help from other people.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.923
Would you be comfortable asking
for informational support,

00:00:34.963 --> 00:00:38.396
such as advice or suggestions,
tangible support,

00:00:38.436 --> 00:00:43.255
such as financial help or help
with tasks, or emotional support,

00:00:43.295 --> 00:00:47.670
such as words or actions that reflect
caring and understanding?

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:52.690
Not everyone is comfortable with all
these types of social support.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:54.190
That is okay.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.010
Do what is right for you.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:02.630
Maybe you are better at giving support
to others rather than receiving it.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:06.261
If so, think about reasons
why people come to you

00:01:06.301 --> 00:01:10.630
for help and the type
of support you provide to them.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:14.591
You might spend a moment thinking
about why you might not feel

00:01:14.631 --> 00:01:19.110
good receiving support,
even if you enjoy providing support.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.874
Recall that in previous
sections we talked about

00:01:22.914 --> 00:01:26.070
fitting or matching the coping
strategy with stress.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:29.870
There is a parallel here about
thinking about who to ask for support.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.435
You have to fit the type
of social support you need

00:01:32.475 --> 00:01:35.830
to the type of support others
are willing to give you.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.502
There are a few aspects
to think about when matching

00:01:38.542 --> 00:01:41.830
the social support with who
you want to ask for help.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:46.030
First, you should figure out
what kind of support you need.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.830
Are you looking for help in addressing
a situation that can be solved?

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:55.010
Is the support I need informational
or tangible to help me solve a problem?

00:01:55.290 --> 00:02:00.170
If so, you are looking for someone who
is really good at solving problems.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:03.414
You will want to fit or match
your requests to someone

00:02:03.454 --> 00:02:06.550
who you know to be good
at solving problems.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.231
Thinking about your tinnitus,

00:02:08.271 --> 00:02:12.590
you occasionally need to vent
your frustration about your tinnitus.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:17.250
In this situation, you are not immediately
looking for a problem to be solved.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:20.550
Expressing frustration
is natural and healthy.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.010
If you are seeking someone
to help you with this,

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.162
look for someone who is a good listener,

00:02:25.202 --> 00:02:29.930
someone who will not immediately start
telling you what you should do about this.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.460
In this case, think about stress
management coping and ask yourself,

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.931
do I need some support right now,
someone to listen to me,

00:02:37.971 --> 00:02:41.870
a person who will understand
my frustrations with tinnitus?

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:45.350
If so, you are looking
for someone who is really good

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.949
at giving you a chance to express
your thoughts, to listen,

00:02:48.989 --> 00:02:53.210
or to just be there for you
and not try to change things.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:59.345
Thus, to summarize the matching concept,
in order to trigger social support coping,

00:02:59.385 --> 00:03:04.390
you will have to be aware of the support
strengths of your social contacts.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:10.470
Think about, what kind of support do
I really need and who can provide it to me?

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:15.570
Again, you will want to match your needs
and your social contacts' strengths.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:19.428
Sometimes, we look
for a particular kind of support

00:03:19.468 --> 00:03:22.490
from a person who is not
able to provide it.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:27.010
But this person may be wonderful
at providing a different type of support.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:31.937
This also is true about social support
that you are asked to provide to others.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:36.428
For example, your spouse or partner
may want emotional support from you,

00:03:36.468 --> 00:03:38.850
but you prefer solving problems.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.906
Or, your adult child wants
financial support from you,

00:03:41.946 --> 00:03:46.590
but you are not interested in providing
that to them at this stage of your life.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:51.470
So you have to ask yourself, what kind
of support am I comfortable providing?

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.610
As the saying goes,
awareness is the first step.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:04:00.190
Awareness of what type of social
support you can give and receive.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:06.528
Remember that asking for support does not
mean that you are dependent on the person,

00:04:06.568 --> 00:04:09.390
especially if that support is short-term.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:14.070
The choice is yours about the extent
and type of the support you ask for.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:18.211
Here are some simple techniques
that will help you ask for support.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.690
Let the person know what you need.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:25.110
If you are busy, leave a phone
message or drop them a note.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:30.590
Be specific about the type of support
and how much support you need.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.635
Try to be aware of your comfort
receiving support,

00:04:33.675 --> 00:04:38.470
as well as the comfort level of the person
who is giving you some support.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.598
If it feels uncomfortable
or does not seem to be working,

00:04:41.638 --> 00:04:46.210
remember that you can stop and seek
support from a different person.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:50.350
If you do receive some help,
it is useful to acknowledge the support.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:56.050
Like any good resource, your support
network needs to be maintained and rewarded.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:05:00.142
Some ways that you can let people
know that you appreciate their efforts

00:05:00.182 --> 00:05:05.690
are acknowledge the support, being
specific about how the person is helping.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:10.310
Provide feedback about how things
turned out after they helped you.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.590
Return the favor when you can.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.103
What kind of support are you
best at providing to others?

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:20.790
But sometimes people are a little
too eager to help you.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:24.469
They may be well-meaning
and genuinely want to support you,

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:27.610
but you may not want or need their help.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:31.813
In such cases, a clearly
stated, no thank you,

00:05:31.853 --> 00:05:35.550
I can take care of this myself, is best.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.750
This type of message is often effective.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.414
A mature person will
appreciate your feedback,

00:05:41.454 --> 00:05:46.350
as this provides them with information
about what you want and need.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:48.993
If you acknowledge their
interest in helping you,

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:53.190
you can help smooth things
over after you tell them no.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:57.267
To summarize this section
on social support coping,

00:05:57.307 --> 00:06:02.670
there may be times that you need to ask
others for some support or assistance.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:04.801
And there will be times
in which you will be

00:06:04.841 --> 00:06:07.050
able to give support
and assistance to others.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:11.599
It would be advisable to think about
your comfort zones in each area,

00:06:11.639 --> 00:06:15.470
that is, in both giving
and receiving social support.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:19.392
As explained in this section,
the type of social support you need should

00:06:19.432 --> 00:06:23.450
match the type of social support
that people are willing to give you.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.515
This is the concept of fitting
or matching the stress

00:06:26.555 --> 00:06:30.270
and the coping technique
as applied to social support.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:33.708
Social support can consist
of either problem-solving support

00:06:33.748 --> 00:06:37.565
or stress management support from others,
not everyone needs this

00:06:37.605 --> 00:06:41.130
kind of support or is comfortable
with giving or receiving it.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:45.330
It is up to you to make those decisions
when dealing with your tinnitus.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:46.899
In the next and final section,

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:51.470
we will go over everything that we
have discussed in this course.
